@comment{
  Publications and working papers go here, newest first.
  jekyll-scholar renders this file onto /publications/.

  NOTE: BibTeX has no line-comment character. Do not use % or #.
  Wrap prose in an @comment{...} block like this one.

  al-folio extras beyond standard BibTeX fields:
    abbr     = {JMP}          small badge beside the entry
    abstract = {...}          adds an expandable "Abs" button
    pdf      = {paper.pdf}    file in assets/pdf/, or a full URL
    selected = {true}         also feature it on the front page
    award    = {...}

  Template to copy:

  @unpublished{brell_jmp,
    title    = {Job Market Paper Title},
    author   = {Brell, Courtney},
    year     = {2026},
    note     = {Job Market Paper},
    abbr     = {JMP},
    abstract = {One paragraph summarising the paper.},
    pdf      = {jmp.pdf},
    selected = {true}
  }
}
